      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3175005275,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Short answer is that the dialog only shows the description and not the name of an interface, if the description is present. In BLF the regular name is what you expect and the description is set to an auto-generated name. This changed in 4.6 and confuses users it seems.\n\nFor the whole discussion you may want to read up here: https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/work_items/21069",
